function(r){const sets=[['oak','pine','maple','rose'],['violin','flute','trumpet','hammer'],['triangle','square','circle','rectangle'],['Mercury','Venus','Mars','Moon'],['sparrow','eagle','penguin','salmon']];const g=r.pick(sets),c=g[3];return mc(`Which item does not belong with the others?`,c,g.slice(0,3),{topic:'Classification',skill:'Identify a shared category',explanation:'Three items share a category that the odd item does not.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const p=r.pick(['P','Q','R','S']),q0=r.pick(['T','U','V','W']);return mc(`Rule: ${p} must occur before ${q0}. Which statement must be true?`,`${p} is before ${q0}`,[`${q0} is before ${p}`,`${p} is immediately before ${q0}`,`${q0} is immediately after ${p}`],{topic:'Ordering',skill:'Identify a necessary condition',explanation:'The rule guarantees only the stated order, not adjacency.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const letters=r.pick([['A','B','C'],['D','E','F'],['P','Q','R','S']]),nums=r.pick([[1,2],[3,4,5],[6,7,8]]),c=letters.length*nums.length;return mc(`A code uses one letter from ${letters.join(', ')} followed by one number from ${nums.join(', ')}. How many codes are possible?`,c,[c+1,c-1,letters.length+nums.length,letters.length*nums.length+2],{topic:'Combinations',skill:'Count independent choices',explanation:'Multiply the number of choices for each independent position.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const rules=[['All red tiles are large.','A large tile is not necessarily red.',['Every large tile is red.','No large tile is red.','Every red tile is small.']],['All musicians can read music.','Being able to read music does not prove someone is a musician.',['Everyone who reads music is a musician.','No musician can read music.','Everyone is a musician.']],['All cedar trees are plants.','Being a plant does not prove that something is a cedar tree.',['Every plant is a cedar tree.','No cedar tree is a plant.','Every cedar tree is an animal.']]];const z=r.pick(rules);return mc(`${z[0]} Which conclusion is safest?`,z[1],z[2],{topic:'Deduction',skill:'Avoid reversing a rule',explanation:'A statement of the form “all A are B” does not prove that all B are A.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const x=r.int(2,9),y=r.int(3,9),z=r.int(4,10),c=z;return mc(`If ${x} → ${x+2} and ${y} → ${y+2}, the rule is “add 2”. What does ${z} become?`,c+2,[c+1,c*2,c-2,c+4],{topic:'Rules',skill:'Generalise a transformation rule',explanation:'Apply the established transformation to the new input.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const p=r.pick(['A','B','C']),q0=r.pick(['D','E','F']),c=`${p} before ${q0}`;return mc(`${p} must be before ${q0}. Which order is possible?`,c,[`${q0} before ${p}`,`${p} after ${q0}`,`${q0} immediately before ${p}`],{topic:'Sequencing',skill:'Test whether an arrangement satisfies a rule',explanation:'A possible order must satisfy the required relative position.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const n=r.int(2,8),c=n*3;return mc(`A machine triples an input. Which input produces ${c}?`,n,[n+3,n*2,c-3,c+3],{topic:'Reverse reasoning',skill:'Work backwards from an output',explanation:'Undo multiplication by dividing the output by the multiplier.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){let a=r.int(3,9),b=r.int(2,8);while(a===b)b=r.int(2,8);return mc(`Exactly one of these statements is true: A says “${a} is greater than ${b}”. B says “${b} is greater than ${a}”. Which statement is true?`,a>b?'A':'B',[a>b?'B':'A','Both','Neither'],{topic:'Logic',skill:'Evaluate mutually exclusive statements',explanation:'Because the two values are different, exactly one of the two comparisons is true.',difficulty:''},r)},
function(r){const odd=r.pick([3,5,7,9]),c=odd;return mc(`Which number completes the pattern? 2, 4, 6, 8, ?`,10,[odd,12,11],{topic:'Sequences',skill:'Recognise a simple numerical rule',explanation:'The pattern increases by 2 each time.',difficulty:'Foundation'},r)},
function(r){const words=[['seed','plant','flower','sun'],['plan','build','test','revise'],['notice','question','investigate','conclude']];const g=r.pick(words),c=g.join(' → ');return mc(`Which sequence shows the most logical process?`,c,[g.slice().reverse().join(' → '),`${g[0]} → ${g[2]} → ${g[1]} → ${g[3]}`,`${g[1]} → ${g[0]} → ${g[3]} → ${g[2]}`],{topic:'Process reasoning',skill:'Order stages logically',explanation:'The best sequence follows the natural dependency between the stages.',difficulty:''},r)},
